 {r}←PrintReleaseCommand parms;notes;cmd;item;buff
⍝ Takes what `CreateRelease` collected and prints the `gh` command that would create
⍝ the release on GitHub.\\
⍝ **Nothing is executed and nothing is sent to GitHub**: the command is printed for you
⍝ to check and then run yourself.\\
⍝ The release notes are written to a temporary file which the command refers to, because
⍝ passing several lines of Markdown on a command line is asking for trouble.\\
⍝ Assets are taken relative to `projectHome`, unless they are absolute already.\\
⍝ Note that `gh` creates the tag if it does not exist yet.\\
⍝ Returns the command as a shy result, so that it can be captured.
 'Right argument must be a namespace'Assert 9=⎕NC'parms'
⍝ What could not be collected is reported first: when something essential is among it
⍝ the checks below signal, and then this report is the only explanation you get.
 :If 0<≢parms.missing
     ⎕←'*** Not collected:'
     :For item :In parms.missing
         ⎕←'      ',item
     :EndFor
     ⎕←''
 :EndIf
 'There is no owner'Assert 0<≢parms.owner
 'There is no repository'Assert 0<≢parms.repo
 'There is no tag'Assert 0<≢parms.tag
 cmd←'gh release create "',parms.tag,'"'
 cmd,←' --repo "',parms.owner,'/',parms.repo,'"'
 :If 0<≢parms.releaseTitle
     cmd,←' --title "',parms.releaseTitle,'"'
 :EndIf
 :If 0<≢parms.body
     notes←'.md'FilesAndDirs.GetTempFilename2'ReleaseNotes'
     (⊂parms.body)⎕NPUT notes 1
     cmd,←' --notes-file "',notes,'"'
 :EndIf
 :If parms.draft
     cmd,←' --draft'
 :EndIf
 :If parms.prerelease
     cmd,←' --prerelease'
 :EndIf
 :If 0<≢parms.target
     cmd,←' --target "',parms.target,'"'
 :EndIf
 :If 0<≢parms.assets
     ⍝ "gh" may well be run from anywhere, so it gets fully qualified names
     buff←(⊂parms.projectHome){(':'∊2↑⍵)∨'/'=⊃⍵:⍵ ⋄ ⍺,'/',⍵}¨parms.assets
     cmd,←⊃,/(⊂' "'),¨buff,¨⊂'"'
 :EndIf
 ⎕←cmd
 r←cmd
⍝Done
